#: ../../source/testing/session_testing.rst:43
msgid "Session Assertions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/session_testing.rst:46
msgid "Using PHPUnit Assertions with ArrayHandler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/session_testing.rst:48
msgid ""
"When testing sessions directly with Session and ArrayHandler in a unit "
"test, use standard PHPUnit assertions. ``assertSessionHas()`` and "
"``assertSessionMissing()`` are not available in this context because you "
"are interacting directly with the session object, not a response object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/session_testing.rst:55
msgid "Session Assertions via TestResponse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/session_testing.rst:57
msgid ""
"When testing controllers or HTTP responses, you can use CodeIgniter 4’s "
"session assertion helpers, such as ``assertSessionHas()`` and "
"``assertSessionMissing()``, which are available on the ``TestResponse`` "
"object. These helpers allow you to assert the state of the session during"
" the HTTP request/response lifecycle. See more: :ref:`Session Assertions "
"<response-session-assertions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/session_testing.rst:64
msgid "Custom Session Values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/session_testing.rst:66
msgid ""
"In Feature Tests, you can provide custom session data for a single test "
"using the ``withSession()`` method. This allows you to simulate session "
"states such as logged-in users or specific roles during the request. For "
"full details and examples, see: :ref:`Setting Session Values <feature-"
"setting-session-values>`"
msgstr ""

